Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");
cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, new SecretKeySpec(secretKey, "AES"), new IvParameterSpec(iv));
```

4. Use the `updateAAD` method to authenticate your data before encrypting it. The `updateAAD` method takes two arguments: the first is the data you want to authenticate, and the second is the length of the data in bytes.

```java
byte[] data = "Your data to be encrypted".getBytes();
int dataLength = data.length;

cipher.updateAAD(data, dataLength);
```

5. Encrypt your data using the `doFinal` method of the cipher object.

```java
byte[] encryptedData = cipher.doFinal(data);
```

6. Base64 encode the encrypted data for storage or transmission.

