def find_max(arr):
    max_value = arr[0]
    for i in range(1, len(arr)):
        if arr[i] > max_value:
            max_value = arr[i]
    return max_value
```

This algorithm initializes the maximum value to the first element of the array. It then iterates through the remaining elements of the array and compares each element with the current maximum value. If an element is greater than the current maximum value, it updates the maximum value to that element. Finally, it returns the maximum value.

