1. First, make sure you have installed `react-native-fbsdk-next` and set up your Facebook app ID in your project.

2. Create a new file called `Authentication.js` and add the following code:
```javascript
import { Facebook } from 'react-native-fbsdk';

const Authentication = () => {
  const handleLogin = async (credentials) => {
    try {
      await Facebook.loginWithCredentialsAsync(credentials);
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Error logging in with Facebook:', error);
    }
  };

  return (
    <Button title="Log in with Facebook" onPress={() => handleLogin({ email: 'your_email@example.com', password: 'your_password' })} />
  );
};

export default Authentication;
```
In this example, we've created a `handleLogin` function that takes an object containing the user's email and password as credentials. The function then calls the `Facebook.loginWithCredentialsAsync` method to log in the user with the provided credentials.

3. Now, you can import the `Authentication` component in your main application file and use it to log in users with their Facebook credentials. For example:
```javascript
import React from 'react';
import { View, Button } from 'react-native';
import Authentication from './Authentication';

const App = () => {
  return (
    <View>
      <Button title="Log in with Facebook" onPress={() => Authentication()} />
    </View>
  );
};

export default App;
```
This will render a button that, when clicked, will open the Facebook login screen and allow the user to log in with their Facebook credentials. The `handleLogin` function will then be called with the user's email and password as credentials.

