First, let's create a MATLAB function to simulate the natural selection process. This function will take as input the initial population, the selection pressure, and the number of generations. It will then simulate the selection process for the specified number of generations and return the final population.

```matlab
function final_population = natural_selection(initial_population, selection_pressure, num_generations)
    % Initialize the final population
    final_population = initial_population;

    % Simulate the natural selection process for the specified number of generations
    for i = 1:num_generations
        % Evaluate the fitness of each individual based on the selection pressure
        fitness = initial_population.BeakSize * initial_population.WingLength .* selection_pressure;

        % Select the individuals with the highest fitness to reproduce
        selected_individuals = initial_population(sort(fitness, 'descend'), :);

        % Create the next generation by randomly combining the genes of the selected individuals
        offspring = cross_over(selected_individuals);

        % Mutate the genes of the offspring with a small probability
        mutation_rate = 0.01;
        offspring = mutate_genes(offspring, mutation_rate);

        % Update the final population with the offspring
        final_population = offspring;
    end
end
```

